description: 
globs: *.mdc
alwaysApply: false
---
# MDC Content Validation Standards

<rule>
name: mdc_content_validation
description: Standards for validating the content structure and format of MDC files
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.mdc$"
  - type: event
    pattern: "file_create|file_modify"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When creating or modifying MDC files:

      1. Required Frontmatter Structure:
         ```yaml
         ---
         description: Brief description of the rule's purpose
         globs: File patterns this rule applies to
         alwaysApply: true/false
         ---
         ```

      2. Rule Content Structure:
         ```markdown
         # Rule Title

         <rule>
         name: rule_name
         description: Detailed description of the rule
         filters:
           - type: filter_type
             pattern: "regex_pattern"
         actions:
           - type: action_type
             message: |
               Detailed message with guidelines
         examples:
           - input: |
               Example input
             output: |
               Expected output
         metadata:
           priority: high/medium/low
           version: "1.0"
         </rule>
         ```

      3. Required Sections:
         - Frontmatter with description, globs, and alwaysApply
         - Title in H1 format
         - Rule block with:
           - name (kebab-case)
           - description
           - filters
           - actions
           - examples
           - metadata

      4. Best Practices:
         - Use clear, descriptive names
         - Include comprehensive examples
         - Keep descriptions concise but informative
         - Use proper markdown formatting
         - Include relevant metadata
         - Test rule with various inputs
         - Document any dependencies

      5. Common Pitfalls to Avoid:
         - Missing frontmatter
         - Incorrect glob patterns
         - Incomplete rule structure
         - Missing examples
         - Poorly formatted markdown
         - Inconsistent naming conventions
         - Missing metadata

examples:
  - input: |
      # My Rule
      This is a rule without proper structure
    output: |
      ---
      description: Standards for my rule
      globs: *.ts
      alwaysApply: true
      ---
      # My Rule

      <rule>
      name: my_rule
      description: Standards for my rule implementation
      filters:
        - type: file_extension
          pattern: "\\.ts$"
      actions:
        - type: suggest
          message: |
            Implementation guidelines here
      examples:
        - input: |
            // Example input
          output: |
            // Expected output
      metadata:
        priority: high
        version: "1.0"
      </rule>

  - input: |
      ---
      description: Rule without proper content
      globs: *.ts
      alwaysApply: true
      ---
      # My Rule
    output: |
      ---
      description: Standards for my rule
      globs: *.ts
      alwaysApply: true
      ---
      # My Rule

      <rule>
      name: my_rule
      description: Standards for my rule implementation
      filters:
        - type: file_extension
          pattern: "\\.ts$"
      actions:
        - type: suggest
          message: |
            Implementation guidelines here
      examples:
        - input: |
            // Example input
          output: |
            // Expected output
      metadata:
        priority: high
        version: "1.0"
      </rule>

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: "1.0"
</rule> 